{"title":"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are primes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac36e406af02bf6555ee54ff421e92be152afb9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-px+q=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> has distinct positive integral roots, then which of the following statements are true? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/63308a5e177b29dda0a38e8532016b92238bafb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I.\\ \\text{The difference of the roots is odd.} \\\\ II.\\ \\text{At least one root is prime.} \\\\ III.\\ p^2-q\\ \\text{is prime}. \\\\ IV.\\ p+q\\ \\text{is prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"265\" height=\"76\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eaee4043d68358def20e070eede389029107a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ \\textbf{(A)}\\ I\\ \\text{only} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ II\\ \\text{only} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ II\\ \\text{and}\\ III\\ \\text{only} \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ I, II, \\text{and}\\ IV\\ \\text{only}\\ \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{All are true.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"46\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the roots are both positive integers, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86033897dda40de295a77bfb92546261b35a3a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-px+q=(x-1)(x-q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"19\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divisors. Thus, the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/074b1196f14be148f818d3466926a9629b24df0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=q+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />. The only two primes which differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e776ea524ca7e92dff794b92acf711ed57cd9367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/2249017892bda0490d89aa6d997b953b070b1ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b419b91958d111b91db52e72a0e8d750e2b23174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is true because one of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which is prime.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a16dd7d1d1fedb353096f50c74ce0da7d1d093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$III$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e4d4119277804a110daff430bb021ebb40a74de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2-2=7$\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> is prime.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77937bd511ef606638c7ac4dc32e42f09545d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51568fcfbf4352db805186994ea99d9cdfdf563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> is prime. \nThus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />.\n-brainiacmaniac31\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1975 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a hr